# Version Alignment Gate

RULE: Quality gates BLOCK if your repo or its dependencies have version drift vs remote staging/main. Pre-commit blocks if you're behind on branch commits. Admin force-sync blocks if remote manifest has bumps your local doesn't have.

WHY: Force-pushing or quickmerging with stale versions can revert remote bumps or create integration conflicts. Three layers catch drift at different stages.

DO: Fix drift before proceeding. Pull latest PM manifest: `cd unified-trading-pm && git pull origin main`. Then run version alignment: `bash unified-trading-pm/scripts/repo-management/run-version-alignment.sh --fix`.

NEVER: Use `--skip-version-alignment` in agent or automated contexts. This flag is human-only.
NEVER: Use `--force-version-override` in agent scripts. This flag is human-only.
NEVER: Use `SKIP_BRANCH_DRIFT=1` in agent commits. This override is human-only.

## Layers
1. **Pre-commit** (`check-branch-drift.sh`): Branch commit drift only. Instant, no network for version check.
2. **Quality gates** (`version-alignment-gate.sh`): Self + dependency version drift vs remote PM manifest. One fetch, ~3s.
3. **Admin force-sync** (safety gate 3): All repos' versions vs remote PM manifest. Blocks force-push to main/staging.
4. **Quickmerge** (stage 1.6): Dependency version canary. Warning only, doesn't block.
